== 2. The Eighteen Samskaras (Ashtadasha-Samskara)
<the-eighteen-samskaras-ashtadasha-samskara>
=== 2.1 Overview
<overview>
The #emph[ashtadasha-samskara] is a sequence of eighteen procedural
transformations applied to mercury, organized in two phases:

#strong[Deha-vada (samskaras 1-8)] — purification for medicinal use.
Currently practiced in licensed Ayurvedic pharmacy. Reproducible.
Produces mercury suitable for incorporation into #emph[kupipakwa
rasayanas], #emph[bhasmas], and other formulations.

#strong[Loha-vada (samskaras 9-18)] — alchemical/transformational
procedures aimed at metal transmutation and bodily immortality. Not
currently practiced in mainstream rasashastra. Some intermediate
substances correspond to real compounds; the ultimate transmutation
claim (gold from base metal) is not supported by modern chemistry.

The split is documented in #emph[Rasaratna Samuccaya] and
#emph[Rasahridayatantra]. The #emph[Ayurveda Prakasha] gives the variant
numerical claim "#emph[ashtadashaiva samskara unavimshatika kvachit]" —
"eighteen samskaras certainly, sometimes nineteen" — acknowledging
textual variants that include or exclude #emph[anuvasana] as a separate
samskara.

