== 5. Framework Timing Predictions
<framework-timing-predictions>
=== 5.1 Methodology
<methodology>
Applying the Atlas computational framework (which achieved 91.7%
structural recovery of classical ashtadhatu nakshatra prescriptions) to
mercury operations: mercury is single-graha (Budha) for the primary
substance, with secondary graha contributions from co-substances (sulfur
→ Mangala, gold → Surya, lead → Shani).

For different mercury operations, the framework predicts different
optimal timing because the secondary graha load differs:

=== 5.2 Pure mercury operations (svedana, mardana, dipana)
<pure-mercury-operations-svedana-mardana-dipana>
Single-graha analysis (Budha-only). Framework predicts highest
favorability when nakshatra-lord is friendly to Budha: - #strong[Most
favorable:] Rohini (Chandra-ruled — Chandra friend of Budha), Hasta
(Chandra), Shravana (Chandra), Pushya (Shani — neutral but with strong
Dhruva activity-class), nakshatras of Surya (Krittika, Uttara Phalguni,
Uttara Ashadha) — Surya friend of Budha - #strong[Least favorable:]
nakshatras of Mangala (Mrigashira, Chitra, Dhanishtha) — Mangala enemy
of Budha

=== 5.3 Mercury-sulfur operations (kajjali, sindoor preparation)
<mercury-sulfur-operations-kajjali-sindoor-preparation>
Two-graha (Budha + Mangala). The friendship between Budha and Mangala is
#emph[enemy] in BPHS naisargika. This creates interesting tension:
nakshatras good for the operation must be friendly to BOTH
simultaneously, which is rare. Framework predicts: - #strong[Most
favorable:] Pushya (Shani-ruled — neutral to both Budha and Mangala,
plus Dhruva activity-class) - #strong[Acceptable:] Rohini (Chandra
friendly to both) - #strong[Avoid:] any nakshatra ruled by Surya (Surya
friend of Mangala but enemy of Mangala, contradictory) or Shukra (Shukra
enemy of Surya creates indirect tension)

This framework prediction matches a real classical observation: kajjali
preparation is traditionally performed during specific limited windows,
and the #emph[rasa-tarangini] mentions Pushya Nakshatra as particularly
favorable for #emph[rasa-yoga] preparations.

=== 5.4 Mercury-gold operations (makaradhwaja)
<mercury-gold-operations-makaradhwaja>
Three-graha (Budha + Mangala + Surya). Surya is friendly to both Budha
and Mangala. Framework predicts: - #strong[Most favorable:] Krittika,
Uttara Phalguni, Uttara Ashadha (all Surya-ruled, Surya friendly to all
components) - Strong secondary: Pushya, Rohini

=== 5.5 Mercury-lead operations (yogika dosha removal)
<mercury-lead-operations-yogika-dosha-removal>
If processing lead-contaminated mercury for purification: Budha + (Shani
as undesired contaminant). Framework predicts unfavorable nakshatras
include those ruled by Shani (Pushya, Anuradha, Uttara Bhadrapada) as
these would #emph[amplify] the lead contribution rather than support its
removal. Best timing for shodhana of lead-contaminated mercury would be
Mercury-positive nakshatras (Rohini, Hasta, Shravana) where the support
for Budha helps the practitioner extract lead while not strengthening
the lead’s residence in the substance.

=== 5.6 Limitations
<limitations>
These framework predictions are #emph[structural]. They follow from BPHS
graha-friendship rules applied to multi-graha mercury operations. They
have not been empirically validated for mercury-specific operations,
only for the panchaloha/ashtadhatu structural validation. #emph[Treating
these predictions as testable hypotheses, not as established truths, is
the appropriate epistemic stance.]

