== 7. Gap Analysis: Tradition vs. Modern Interpretation
<gap-analysis-tradition-vs.-modern-interpretation>
=== 7.1 Where the tradition is correct
<where-the-tradition-is-correct>
- #strong[Mercury has multiple toxicity modes] (visha, vahni) —
  accurately observed
- #strong[Mercury has source-derived contaminants] (yogika doshas, naga,
  vanga) — accurately observed
- #strong[Surface oxidation produces dosha-like clinical effects] (sapta
  kanchuka) — accurately observed; described symptoms match mercury
  poisoning
- #strong[Processing reduces bioavailability] — accurately observed; HgS
  is less bioavailable than Hg⁰ or Hg²⁺
- #strong[Mercury forms compounds with sulfur, gold, mica with specific
  characteristics] — accurately described
- #strong[Specific timing-related observations about mercury’s behavior]
  — partially accurate; depend on factors the framework can encode

=== 7.2 Where the tradition’s claims are not supported
<where-the-traditions-claims-are-not-supported>
- #strong[Element-level transmutation of base metals to gold] — not
  possible at chemical energies
- #strong[Bodily immortality through mercury consumption] — not
  supported; chronic mercury exposure causes the opposite
- #strong[Eight inherent doshas → mercury can be made completely safe] —
  not supported; mercury accumulates regardless of preparation
- #strong[Specific weight conservation claims in jarana] — not validated
  by modern reproduction
- #strong["Mercury sees its true nature only in proper hands"] —
  esoteric claim, not chemistry

=== 7.3 Where the framework can help
<where-the-framework-can-help>
- #strong[Identifying which intermediate substances are real] — Atlas’s
  recovery model framework distinguishes "real chemistry under
  cosmological framing" from "aspirational/symbolic"
- #strong[Predicting timing-dependent variation] — single-moment
  framework prediction for any mercury operation
- #strong[Cross-referencing with practitioner-state] — natal chart
  compatibility for the operator
- #strong[Documenting what’s actually being produced] — independent of
  the tradition’s claims about it

