== 8. Empirical Research Targets
<empirical-research-targets>
=== 8.1 Highest-leverage experimental tests
<highest-leverage-experimental-tests>
If empirical validation work were possible:

+ #strong[Yashada-bhasma timing study] — yashada-bhasma has published
  nano-particle measurements (Singh et al., similar to swarnabhasma).
  Producing yashada-bhasma on framework-favorable vs. unfavorable
  nakshatras and comparing nano-particle morphology, size distribution,
  surface chemistry would directly test the framework’s timing
  predictions. Equipment: TEM, DLS, XRD (~\$100K capital but available
  at any university materials lab). #emph[Note: yashada is zinc, not
  mercury — listed here because it’s the cleanest test, mercury
  preparations have toxicity barriers.]

+ #strong[Sindoor color analysis] — Production of sindoor (α-HgS) on
  different framework-predicted dates, with spectrophotometric color
  analysis. The α-HgS color depends on crystallite size and defect
  density; framework prediction is that timing affects these. Equipment:
  UV-vis spectrophotometer (~\$5K). #emph[Equipment cost is low enough
  to be feasible.]

+ #strong[Kajjali completion-time study] — Time to achieve
  #emph[nishchandratva] (complete Hg+S reaction) on framework-favorable
  vs. unfavorable nakshatras. Framework predicts faster completion on
  favorable nakshatras due to Budha-Mangala being mediated through
  favorable nakshatra-lord. Equipment: timer and weighing.
  #emph[Effectively zero equipment cost.]

=== 8.2 Realistic constraints
<realistic-constraints>
- #strong[Mercury handling regulations] restrict where this work can be
  done
- #strong[Statistical power] requires multiple batches per condition;
  mercury preparations are time-consuming
- #strong[Reproducibility] of traditional methods varies between
  practitioners
- #strong[Confounding variables] (practitioner skill, ambient
  temperature, humidity, equipment) need controlling

A serious empirical program would require partnership with a licensed
Ayurvedic college that has both the materials infrastructure and the
practitioner expertise. #emph[Government Ayurvedic College Patiala,
IPGT&RA Jamnagar, AIIA New Delhi] are among the institutions where such
work could feasibly be initiated.

